}
\HLAStableID{m4.p041.b02}
\HLAClausePlacedBlock{90.000}{610.805}{432.065}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{432.008bp}{!}{\mbox{In all HLA object models, any object class that is referenced in any table within the object model shall also}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.065bp}{!}{\mbox{be included in the object class hierarchy. The criteria for designing an object class hierarchy for an HLA}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.999bp}{!}{\mbox{object model is fundamentally different for individual federates than for federations. The object class}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.020bp}{!}{\mbox{structure table of a FOM or FOM module represents an agreement between the federates in a federation on}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.022bp}{!}{\mbox{how to classify object classes for the purposes of federation executions. The object class structure table of a}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.982bp}{!}{\mbox{SOM or SOM module is a type of advertisement of the classes of objects that the federate can support (as}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.978bp}{!}{\mbox{Publish or Subscribe) in potential federations. In neither case does the HLA require specific object classes}}\newline{}\resizebox{419.169bp}{!}{\mbox{(other than the required root class) or object class hierarchies to appear in the object class structure table.}}}
}
