\HLAClausePlacedBlock{89.999}{478.805}{432.075}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{432.002bp}{!}{\mbox{Each class of simulation domain objects shall be characterized by a set of attribute types and dimensions.}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.010bp}{!}{\mbox{For a given, named object class, several FOM/SOM modules may provide attributes and dimensions. These}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.075bp}{!}{\mbox{attributes are named portions of their object’s state whose values can change over time (such as location or}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.018bp}{!}{\mbox{velocity of a platform). The values of HLA instance attributes are updated through the RTI and provided to}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.943bp}{!}{\mbox{other federates in a federation. Both federates and federations shall document all such object attributes in the}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.998bp}{!}{\mbox{attribute table of their SOM, FOM, and relevant SOM modules and FOM modules. The object class}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.986bp}{!}{\mbox{“HLAobjectRoot” shall be a superclass of all other object classes in a FOM or FOM module and in a SOM}}\newline{}\resizebox{303.122bp}{!}{\mbox{or SOM module; attributes may be assigned to it like any other object class.}}}
}
\HLAStableID{m4.p047.b13}
\HLAClausePlacedBlock{90.001}{586.803}{432.038}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{432.008bp}{!}{\mbox{Attributes of HLA object classes are specified in order to support subscription to their values by other}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.025bp}{!}{\mbox{interested members of a federation. Thus, the names of attributes and associated object classes are essential}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.011bp}{!}{\mbox{information when initializing a federation execution. Knowledge of object attributes is commonly required}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.986bp}{!}{\mbox{for effective communication between federates in a federation. In addition, although the data types and}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.994bp}{!}{\mbox{update policies of attributes represent characteristics that are not directly utilized by the RTI, they are}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.971bp}{!}{\mbox{important to ensuring compatibility among federates in a federation. A federate operating with very low}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.015bp}{!}{\mbox{update rates for an instance attribute could create problems for interacting federates that are operating at}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.982bp}{!}{\mbox{high update rates. The specification of data types and update rates in an HLA FOM is a part of the FOM}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.037bp}{!}{\mbox{“contract” among federates to interoperate at the specified levels. These specifications provide a common}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.038bp}{!}{\mbox{perception of the simulation space across federates in a federation, lowering the potential for inconsistency.}}}
}
