\HLAClausePlacedBlock{90.000}{261.783}{432.037}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{431.985bp}{!}{\mbox{Table 11 shows examples of attributes from the restaurant application described in 4.2.4. First, the\space{}\textit{Employee}}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.037bp}{!}{\mbox{object class is characterized according to the four attributes shown in the table. The data types specified are}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.984bp}{!}{\mbox{defined in the examples provided in 4.14. Each of these four attributes is updated conditionally except for}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.958bp}{!}{\mbox{the\space{}\textit{YearsOfService}\space{}attribute, which is updated periodically (yearly) on the employee’s start date}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.019bp}{!}{\mbox{anniversary. A value is required for PayRate and YearsOfService, but it is optional to provide a value for}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.984bp}{!}{\mbox{HomeNumber and HomeAddress. As with most of the domain-specific attributes shown in this example, the}}\newline{}\resizebox{359.258bp}{!}{\mbox{attributes of\space{}\textit{Employee}\space{}are assumed divestable, acquirable, publishable, and subscribable.}}}
}
