\HLAStableID{m4.p065.b03}
\HLAClausePlacedBlock{90.000}{118.805}{432.077}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{432.077bp}{!}{\mbox{The HLA RTI performs actions on behalf of federates. Some of these actions may be enabled or disabled}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.982bp}{!}{\mbox{based on the capabilities of the federates or desires of the federation designers. These actions include}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.989bp}{!}{\mbox{automatically soliciting updates of instance attribute values when an object is newly discovered (controlled}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.988bp}{!}{\mbox{by the\space{}\textit{Auto Provide}\space{}switch\textit{)}; and advising federates when certain events occur (controlled by the advisory}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.017bp}{!}{\mbox{switches). The switches table permits the specification of the initial setting of each switch, indicating}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.923bp}{!}{\mbox{whether the RTI should perform these actions. The functionality of these switches is described fully in IEEE}}\newline{}\resizebox{69.094bp}{!}{\mbox{Std 1516.1-2025.}}}
}
\HLAStableID{m4.p065.b04}
\HLAClausePlacedBlock{89.999}{214.804}{432.068}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{432.001bp}{!}{\mbox{Although the initial setting of each switch can be specified in this table, the value of each switch, excluding}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.986bp}{!}{\mbox{static switches, may be changed during execution. Some switches are managed on a per-federate basis. In}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.973bp}{!}{\mbox{such cases, each federate in a federation gets its initial settings from the RTI, as described in 4.1.4.3 of IEEE}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.039bp}{!}{\mbox{Std 1516.1-2025. A change to a per-federate switch setting is specified for an individual federate and the}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.948bp}{!}{\mbox{change only affects how the RTI interacts with that federate. For example, the RTI initializes each federate}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.967bp}{!}{\mbox{to report service invocations or not, as indicated by the\space{}\textit{Service Reporting}\space{}switch found in this table; a}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.068bp}{!}{\mbox{federate making a change to this switch setting on another federate affects whether the RTI reports service}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.045bp}{!}{\mbox{invocations for the specified federate. The per-federate switches are\space{}\textit{Attribute Relevance Advisory, Attribute}}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.011bp}{!}{\mbox{\textit{Scope Advisory, Convey Region Designators, Exception Reporting, Interaction Relevance Advisory, Object}}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.970bp}{!}{\mbox{\textit{Class Relevance Advisory, Automatic Resign Action, Service Reporting,}\space{}and\space{}\textit{Send Service Reports To File}.}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.869bp}{!}{\mbox{The remaining switches are managed on a per-federation basis and the values of these switches are the same}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.039bp}{!}{\mbox{for all federates in a federation. Some of these switches are dynamic and some are static. For the per-}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.018bp}{!}{\mbox{federation dynamic switch,\space{}\textit{Auto Provide}, a federate making a change to this switch setting affects how the}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.930bp}{!}{\mbox{RTI interacts with all federates in the execution. Finally, the\space{}\textit{Delay Subscription Evaluation, Advisories Use}}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.967bp}{!}{\mbox{\textit{Known Class, Allow Relaxed DDM}\space{}and\space{}\textit{Non-Regulated Grant}\space{}are per-federation static switches. The values}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.011bp}{!}{\mbox{for these switches are established when a federation execution is created and they cannot be changed during}}\newline{}\resizebox{41.304bp}{!}{\mbox{execution.}}}
}
\HLAStableID{m4.p065.b05}
