\HLAClausePlacedBlock{90.001}{566.822}{432.025}{%
  \HLAClauseParagraph{\resizebox{432.022bp}{!}{\mbox{Each of the constructed data types (arrays, fixed records, and variant records) has a predefined encoding that}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.018bp}{!}{\mbox{describes how the components (i.e., elements of an array, or fields of a fixed or variant record) within the}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.024bp}{!}{\mbox{constructed data type are laid out with respect to each other. These encodings are defined precisely in the}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.021bp}{!}{\mbox{appropriate subclauses (4.14.10.1 through 4.14.10.5). These predefined encoding definitions include a}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.906bp}{!}{\mbox{description of how each component in a constructed data type shall be padded in order to ensure proper byte}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.990bp}{!}{\mbox{alignment of the component that follows it. The use of any of the predefined keywords\space{}\textit{HLAfixedArray,}}}\newline{}\resizebox{432.006bp}{!}{\mbox{\textit{HLAvariableArray, HLAfixedRecord,}\space{}or\space{}\textit{HLAextendableVariantRecord}\space{}to describe the encoding for a}}\newline{}\resizebox{431.952bp}{!}{\mbox{constructed data type shall indicate adherence to these padding requirements. Object modelers may define}}\newline{}\resizebox{194.500bp}{!}{\mbox{and use alternative encoding schemes as needed.}}}
}
